<h1>quad trie</h1>
<p>
(data structure)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="tree.html"><em>tree</em></a> in which each <a href="node.html"><em>node</em></a> is split according to some subset of the <a href="key.html"><em>key</em></a>, typically a character.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="quadtree.html"><em>quadtree</em></a>, <a href="digitaltree.html"><em>digital tree</em></a>, <a href="patriciatree.html"><em>Patricia tree</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
After <a href="../terms.html#GBY91">[GBY91, pages 146-149]</a>. </p> 
<p> The name comes from re<strong>TRIE</strong>val and is pronounced, "tree".  See the historical note at <a href="trie.html"><em>trie</em></a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
<a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/3/351b.ins.c" target="_blank">insert (C)</a>, <a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/3/351b.srch.c" target="_blank">search (C)</a>

